response.text:
{
  "reviews": [
    {
      "actor": "ash-3",
      "decision": "reuse",
      "ability": "bark-extraction",
      "reason": "The implemented capability already provides the requested physical function: assess actual material and peel a finite outer layer from an owned branch using a personally inspected stone or flint contact. Your stones are potential reusable tools, not automatically validated ones. The observed tree exposes branch stock, not harvestable trunk bark; gathering branches depletes that actual stock. Peeling produces conserved bark and residual core rather than relabeling whole branches. Available material must actually yield the tray's required bark quantity; this review supplies neither bark nor mastery.",
      "specification": "Reuse bark-extraction unchanged; consult its full public contract for action parameters and individually learn it before use. Its existing assessment operation costs one round and 0.2 energy. Peeling requires actual eligible branch material and an inspected reusable stone/flint contact, with two active work-round equivalents and two energy per original branch unit, proportionally reduced for fractional or partly processed material. Use the existing ownership, tool reservation, source provenance, finite-layer and output rules: unspecified intact branches partition at most 10% of existing mass into outer bark; exact-tenth bark units round down and remaining sub-unit material remains bark-fines. Do not infer peelable tissue on standing trunks. Preserve existing shared reference parameters, inventory interactions, reachable-work geometry, progress and completion validation. Cancellation, including death, must retain actual partial work and return or expose each reserved tool and remaining material exactly once under the existing ownership rules, without duplication or deletion. No new interface, resource, geometry or migration is required.",
      "experienceReview": "Reuse existing feedback rather than register an alias. An actual qualifying assessment experiment may emit information-confirmed through bark-extraction and activate grounded-understanding only when it establishes new verified information: amount 0.8, cap 1, duration 8, refresh repetition and cooldown 12; maintained gain 0.035 with decay 0.0015 under the registered rule. Paid, completed processing may emit qualified practice-confirmed for the existing limited progress milestones: amount 0.4, cap 0.5, duration 8, refresh repetition and cooldown 12; maintained gain 0.02 with decay 0.001. Neither requesting, learning, mere completion without a qualifying milestone, nor mastery earns feedback. Repeated known observations do not become new discoveries. No additional pleasure or sustained-satisfaction source is justified separately from these existing functional sources, and nutrition, health and physical comfort remain unchanged.",
      "visualReview": "Reuse bark-assessed, bark-peeling-started, bark-peeling-progress, bark-peeling-completed and bark-peeling-stopped event bindings. Presentation and replay must show the inspected material, actual paid progress, diminishing outer layer, retained core and conserved bark/fines quantities from authoritative state. Show interruption and remaining work without depicting an unearned completed product. No tree damage, bark inventory, drying tray or comfort effect should appear unless the corresponding physical operation actually produces it.",
      "learning": 2
    }
  ]
}

